---
const steps = [
  ['01', 'Session launch', 'A cXML buyer connection starts PunchOut from procurement and opens the configured supplier catalog.'],
  ['02', 'Cart return', 'The selected cart returns to procurement for the buyer’s approval. No Shopify order is created at this point.'],
  ['03', 'Approved PO', 'PunchOut Central connects the approved purchase order to the buyer and earlier cart.'],
  ['04', 'Supplier order', 'The approved PO creates the corresponding Shopify order, with invoice activity visible later in the transaction.']
];
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview"><div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal"><span class="ey">Shopify cXML PunchOut</span><h1>Connect cXML procurement workflows to Shopify.</h1><p class="lead">PunchOut Central supports cXML buyer connections while your existing Shopify or Shopify Plus store remains the supplier catalog. The returned cart goes through buyer approval before a store order is created.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss cXML requirements &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#flow">Follow the flow &darr;</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Procurement protocol</span><b>cXML</b></div><div class="logo-hero__mark"><strong>cXML</strong></div><span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span><h3>Buyer to supplier</h3><p>Protocol support for PunchOut and procurement transactions.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">Connection roles</span><h2>cXML is the protocol, not the storefront.</h2><p class="lead">The buyer uses a procurement system; the supplier uses Shopify. PunchOut Central connects their configured workflow.</p></div>
    <div class="integration-flow reveal"><div class="integration-node"><strong>Buyer procurement</strong><span>cXML connection</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>Session and transaction</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify</strong><span>Supplier catalog and order</span></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="details"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">cXML workflow</span><h2>Keep cart selection separate from the approved order.</h2><p class="lead">The connection is configured and tested for each buyer’s requirements.</p></div>
    <div class="simple-steps">{steps.map(([number, title, description]) => <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Implementation scope</span><h2>Confirm the buyer configuration before launch.</h2><p class="lead">The procurement system, buyer credentials, catalog access, cart return and purchase-order handling should be checked with the buyer during onboarding.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/procurement-systems/"><span>Buyer side</span><h3>Procurement systems</h3><p>Review the buyer ecosystem and connection planning.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/shopify/"><span>Supplier side</span><h3>Shopify integration</h3><p>See how the existing store serves the catalog and orders.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/oci/"><span>Another protocol</span><h3>OCI PunchOut</h3><p>Review the OCI catalog launch and cart-return path.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="faq"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>cXML questions</h2></div>
    <div class="faq reveal"><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does PunchOut Central support cXML?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. cXML PunchOut is live: setup request, catalog launch, cart return, approved PO to Shopify order, and invoice activity.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is setup included?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. Standard supported integration setup and onboarding are included at no extra charge. Buyer-specific custom development is separate.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is cXML a buyer platform?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. cXML is a procurement communication protocol. The buyer’s procurement system and its configuration determine the connection requirements.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does the buyer pay in Shopify checkout?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. The selected cart returns to procurement for approval; the approved PO leads to the Shopify order.</p></div></div><div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is buyer-specific testing needed?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Yes. Confirm the buyer’s settings and test the session, cart return and PO flow before launch.</p></div></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Plan a cXML connection</span><h2>Bring the buyer’s cXML requirements.</h2><p class="lead">Review the procurement system, Shopify catalog and transaction steps together.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss the connection &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/how-it-works/">See the full workflow</a></div></div></section>
</main>
